From 24fd17f911f1ac681735df1f80ebd382effc5041 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:16:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(worker): anchor and atomically release contiguous CUDA
 pool on fallback

Base: vLLM 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus the candidate-73
series (0001..0868).

Rationale:
1. On PP>1 last stages (such as PP1 in pp2-tp2-ring), GPUModelRunner.__init__
   initializes the speculator and sampler before _preallocate_contiguous_cuda_pool()
   runs, leaving >512 MiB of cached-free memory in earlier PyTorch caching-allocator
   segments. _allocate_soaked_contiguous_pool() only drained up to 256 x 2 MiB
   (512 MiB) and fell back to anchoring an arbitrary holder outside
   [pool_ptr, pool_end). Under PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=garbage_collection_threshold:0.6,
   the unanchored 77.5 GiB pool segment was evicted before weight loading.
2. _resize_contiguous_cuda_pool_for_model() then took its Keeping fast path
   without verifying cached_free_bytes >= model_bytes, and bind_weight_arena()
   fell back to allocating a multi-GiB buddy sponge plus weight arena without
   first releasing _contiguous_pool_anchor -- risking double allocation when
   an anchor pins a smaller segment or triggering compaction stalls on fallback.
3. Drain stale cached-free segments with torch.accelerator.empty_cache() before
   allocating the soaked pool, widen the anchor drain loop to 1024 x 2 MiB, and
   raise RuntimeError rather than silently anchoring an unrelated segment.
4. Register Worker._release_contiguous_cuda_pool as release_cb with
   direct_loader.set_preallocated_cuda_pool_bytes so any fallback in
   bind_weight_arena() atomically evacuates and releases the pre-allocated pool
   before buddy-sponge allocation. Gate both Keeping fast paths in
   _resize_contiguous_cuda_pool_for_model() on actual cached_free_bytes >= model_bytes.
5. In _compute_desired_pool_bytes(), skip the draft_and_other reservation on
   non-last PP ranks (pp_size > 1 and not is_last_rank), which hold no drafter.

Quality:
Bit-identical outputs; changes only CUDA caching-allocator pool anchoring,
sizing, and fallback cleanup during model startup.

Tests:
117/117 passed on GB10 (test_contiguous_cuda_pool.py including 3 new regression
tests, test_direct_loader.py, test_direct_loader_cuda.py, test_engine_grid_sync.py).

Upstream-status: Local deployment patch pending upstream submission.
